 "deductions:contradictions.c_dragan_key.insight": "Dragan says Viktor was trusted with the service key, but the club rule allowed only officials to sign it out and the return line is blank.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_dragan_key.response.0": "I made a practical decision. Viktor knew the building and had used that corridor for years.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_dragan_key.response.1": "The rule says only arbiters and the club president may sign out SERVICE 2.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_dragan_key.response.2": "Then I should have stopped him. I did not think a key for the courtyard would matter.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_dragan_key.response.3": "Dragan admits he gave Viktor access, but the key record still points away from Dragan and toward the person who signed it out.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_dragan_key.title": "The badge was not permission",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_attendance.insight": "Elena needed a full event for the city grant, but the attendance ledger shows the final round was not yet underway and the missing signatures were already known.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_attendance.response.0": "I needed the final round to happen. That does not mean I needed Boris silenced.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_attendance.response.1": "You wrote that Boris must not cancel the ceremony, while the attendance sheet was short by seven signatures.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_attendance.response.2": "He was going to give me an hour to collect them. I was at the sponsor table, not behind his stage.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_attendance.response.3": "Elena had public pressure and a fragile grant, but her own paperwork keeps her in the foyer.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_elena_attendance.title": "The missing signatures",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_nikola_break.insight": "Nikola’s photographs place him in the public hall during the break, but his notes show that he was following Boris’s private appeal and knew a document was expected.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_nikola_break.response.0": "I wanted the story, not a body. My camera never went behind the stage.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_nikola_break.response.1": "You knew Boris had a sealed document and that it concerned Viktor.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_nikola_break.response.2": "Knowing a story is coming is not the same as owning it. I was waiting for the final round.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_nikola_break.response.3": "Nikola had a reason to watch Boris, but his time-stamped photographs keep him in the open hall.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_nikola_break.title": "The camera was in public",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_sara_result.insight": "Sara says the replacement slip was already on the board when she returned, but Boris’s desk ledger shows he was reviewing that exact slip before the break ended.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_sara_result.response.0": "I did not write the 1–0. I only saw it after I came back from the foyer.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_sara_result.response.1": "Boris had the replacement under the signed sheet, and your bell log says you checked the stage at 17:52. You knew he was challenging it.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_sara_result.response.2": "I knew he was checking a result. I did not know he had hidden the appeal, and I was afraid to admit I had let the slip reach the board.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_sara_result.response.3": "Sara hid a paperwork mistake, but the records do not place her in the service corridor during the death window.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_sara_result.title": "The correction she did not mention",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_viktor_alibi.insight": "Viktor says he stayed in the analysis room, but his notebook describes the altered demonstration position and his jacket was missing when the service key was out. The café receipt places him outside at 18:08.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_viktor_alibi.response.0": "I left for coffee after six. The notebook does not say I was sitting there every second.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_viktor_alibi.response.1": "Your 18:06 note describes pieces moved on the demonstration board, and your jacket was missing when SERVICE 2 was out.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_viktor_alibi.response.2": "I looked at the board before I left. Someone else could have moved the pieces after me.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_viktor_alibi.response.3": "Viktor’s alibi has become a story about being nearby, not proof that he stayed in the analysis room.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_viktor_alibi.title": "The empty chair",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_viktor_result.insight": "The signed sheet records a draw, while the later 1–0 slip uses Viktor’s squared-off V and agrees with the altered position on the demonstration board.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_viktor_result.response.0": "I corrected nothing. The board was already wrong when I saw it.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_viktor_result.response.1": "The signed sheet says a draw. The replacement slip and the altered demonstration position both favour Maja.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_viktor_result.response.2": "Maja was winning the game in every meaningful sense. A careless result slip should not erase that.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_viktor_result.response.3": "Viktor’s explanation turns a signed result into a matter of opinion. Boris’s appeal says the opposite: the record must follow the board, not a coach’s judgement.",
 "deductions:contradictions.c_viktor_result.title": "Not a copied result",
 "deductions:deductions.d_record.conclusion": "Board Four ended as a signed draw at 17:38. A later unsigned slip changed it to a win for Maja and was placed on the results board during the break. Boris was reviewing the alteration when he died.",
